$DIR/main.p:13:3: p holds a view of a (a.New[int](), line 11), which was reclaimed by a.Reset() at line 12, so p can no longer be used here
    p looks at memory that a owns, without owning it: the view was made by
    a.New[int]() at line 11. A view of a local arena's memory may be used only
    until Reset or Release reclaims it. At line 12 a was reclaimed by a.Reset(),
    so the view may look at memory that was released, or at a value that now
    belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use p before line 12, or call a.Reset() only after the last use of p
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)

